{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nADR 0100 makes the immutable route registry and parser factories the authority for command identity, grammar, and committed help. Twenty-one visible pure-intercept routes support `rebar <command> --help` but remain absent from overview help and fail under `rebar help <command>`.\n\n## Plan\n- Make the existing help-backed predicate in `scripts/gen_cli_help.py` and `src/rebar/_cli/_help_route.py` exactly `not route.hidden and not route.retired`; do not add a Route metadata field. This includes all twenty-one canonical pure-intercept routes while continuing to exclude hidden aliases and retired spellings.\n- Mirror that census in `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py::_routable_subcommands` by removing its `group != \"intercept\"` filter, so routable routes and pinned artifacts remain equal.\n- Add concise parser `description=` values to the four pure-intercept factories that currently lack them: `reconcile.build`, `enrich.build`, `identity.build`, and `certs.build_trusted_env`. These route-owned descriptions supply the required overview one-liners without adding registry metadata or a second prose source.\n- Move `_unwrap_usage` and `_collapse_metavars` from `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` into `scripts/gen_cli_help.py`. In `render_route`, apply `_unwrap_usage` only when `route.group == \"intercept\"` and `parser.usage is None`; this normalizes argparse-generated wrapping but preserves explicit multiline usage. Apply `_collapse_metavars` to intercept option-invocation lines, then use the existing byte normalization.\n- Pin the explicit-usage exception with `trusted-env`: its author-supplied `add` and `revoke` usage forms remain on two lines in the committed artifact. Other pure-intercept artifacts normalize argparse-generated usage across Python versions.\n- Generate one committed `help/<route>.txt` artifact for each newly help-backed intercept route. The existing `src/rebar/_cli/_help.py` file lookup, `subcommand_help`, and `known_subcommands` then serve and discover those files without a second rendering path.\n- Update `_help_route.pre_scan` through its mirrored help-backed predicate so leading or top-level pure-intercept help is served before execution. Keep `_NESTED_FAMILY` behavior unchanged: `rebar bridge preview --help` and `rebar audit serve --help` still fall through to their nested argparse owners, while `rebar audit --help` remains top-level committed help.\n- Delete the live pure-intercept `_render_intercept` path in `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py`; make `_syntax_body` use `help_mod.subcommand_help(route.name)` for every documented route and fail if the committed artifact is absent.\n- Migrate both direct `_render_intercept` consumers in `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py`: assert the `review-plan` `--retry` option and rendered syntax against `help_mod.subcommand_help(\"review-plan\")` or `_syntax_body`, then assert that exact committed body occurs in `render()`. Confirm no remaining semantic or string references to `_render_intercept`.\n- Retain `_OVERVIEW_OMIT` as exactly `bridge-fsck` and `bridge-probe`, the existing compatibility entrypoints already advertised under `bridge`. Retain the matching overview-test allowlist as exactly `help`, `bridge-fsck`, and `bridge-probe`; none of the twenty-one pure-intercept routes is exempted.\n- Keep `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_parser_formatter_pinned.py` scoped away from pure-intercept parsers and update its rationale: those parsers may use stdlib `HelpFormatter` because the committed-help generator performs the cross-version normalization.\n- Regenerate package help, overview help, and the CLI reference through the existing generators.\n- Use the existing `_build-and-test.yml` Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13 matrix. Each cell runs the help drift check against the same committed artifacts, providing the cross-version byte oracle without a provider-specific new gate.\n- Add registry-driven behavioral coverage for every pure-intercept route, exact-byte equality across both top-level help surfaces, generator determinism, factory-summary completeness, reference consumption, the explicit-usage exception, and preserved nested-help fallthrough.\n- Do not add another router, parser, help source, mechanical writing-policy gate, or change to the Markdown-only reduced test policy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every live visible route outside the exact documented overview omit set appears exactly once in overview help.\n- [ ] `rebar help <command>` succeeds for every canonical pure-intercept route returned by the registry.\n- [ ] The registry-driven pure-intercept help test proves no command handler executes.\n- [ ] The registry-driven pure-intercept help test proves no ticket store is mounted or created.\n- [ ] `rebar help <command>` returns the exact bytes of the matching committed route artifact.\n- [ ] Top-level `rebar <command> --help` returns the exact bytes of the matching committed route artifact.\n- [ ] Every pure-intercept parser factory supplies a non-blank overview description.\n- [ ] The committed `trusted-env` usage banner preserves separate `add` and `revoke` lines.\n- [ ] Python 3.11 matrix execution passes `python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check`.\n- [ ] Python 3.12 matrix execution passes `python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check`.\n- [ ] Python 3.13 matrix execution passes `python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check`.\n- [ ] Each CLI-reference pure-intercept syntax block equals the matching committed artifact.\n- [ ] No `_render_intercept` semantic reference remains.\n- [ ] No `_render_intercept` string reference remains.\n- [ ] `_routable_subcommands()` uses the same live-visible census as committed help generation.\n- [ ] `_OVERVIEW_OMIT` retains only `bridge-fsck` and `bridge-probe`.\n- [ ] The overview-test allowlist retains only `help`, `bridge-fsck`, and `bridge-probe`.\n- [ ] Hidden aliases remain absent from overview discovery.\n- [ ] Retired spellings remain absent from overview discovery.\n- [ ] Non-leading `bridge` child help retains argparse fallthrough.\n- [ ] Non-leading `audit` child help retains argparse fallthrough.\n- [ ] The help drift check passes.\n- [ ] The CLI-reference drift check passes.\n- [ ] No competing routing, parser, or help mechanism is introduced.\n- [ ] No mechanical writing enforcement is introduced.\n- [ ] The Markdown-only reduced test policy remains unchanged."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787420123375593001,"uuid":"ad529aa7-d4eb-438f-881b-86ea96439e05"}